  "setup.phase.basics": "The basics",
  "setup.phase.basics.why": "Add your members, invite your team, and set up your church.",
  "setup.phase.before": "Get ready for your service day",
  "setup.phase.before.why": "Set up everything you need for your first service.",
  "setup.phase.running": "Plan your services",
  "setup.phase.running.why": "Organise volunteers, service schedules, and groups.",
  "setup.phase.ready": "More ways to connect",
  "setup.phase.ready.why": "Set up communication, giving, and follow-ups when you are ready.",
  "setup.step.members": "Add your members",
  "setup.what.members": "Upload a CSV or Excel file with your congregation's names and contact details. We'll automatically match the columns, or you can add people individually.",
  "setup.why.members": "Add people once, and their information is available across groups, check-in, volunteer scheduling, giving, reports, and much more.",
  "setup.at.members": "Drop a file here, or press Choose file. We show you what would change and wait for your go-ahead. To add somebody by hand instead, close this and press Add a member.",
  "setup.step.services": "Your first service",
  "setup.what.services": "Add your church services and set the day and time each one takes place.",
  "setup.why.services": "Use these services to track attendance, check in children, and schedule volunteers.",
  "setup.at.services": "Click Create a service, then enter its name, date, and time. Choose whether it repeats.",
  "setup.step.roles": "Set up your roles",
  "setup.what.roles": "Choose from ready-made roles like Admin, Staff, or Pastoral, or create your own.",
  "setup.why.roles": "Roles control what each person can see and do. Set them up before inviting your team.",
  "setup.at.roles": "Click Add a new role, choose a ready-made role or create your own, then save.",
  "setup.step.team": "Invite your team",
  "setup.what.team": "Give pastors, staff, and volunteers access to help manage your church.",
  "setup.why.team": "Choose what each person can see and manage. This keeps responsibilities shared and sensitive information private.",
  "setup.at.team": "Click Invite team member and enter their email address. They'll receive an invitation to set up their own password.",
  "setup.step.church": "Church information",
  "setup.what.church": "Add your church's name, address, country, time zone, and other details.",
  "setup.why.church": "These details appear on giving receipts, help with check-in, and ensure services are scheduled at the correct times.",
  "setup.at.church": "Click Edit, add or update your church's information, then save your changes.",
  "setup.step.rooms": "Rooms for check-in",
  "setup.what.rooms": "One room per class, with the ages it takes and a colour of its own.",
  "setup.why.rooms": "Check-in asks which room a child goes to. The colour prints on the label, so a volunteer can point a parent down the corridor without reading anything.",
  "setup.at.rooms": "Press Add room. Name it the way your church already says it, and give it an age range.",
  "setup.step.stations": "A check-in station",
  "setup.what.stations": "The desk families check in at, and which rooms and services it covers.",
  "setup.why.stations": "A station is what a tablet by the door becomes. It prints the matching label pair that gets the right child back to the right adult, and it keeps working when the wifi does not.",
  "setup.at.stations": "Press Pair a station, name the desk, and tick the rooms it checks into.",
  "setup.step.portal": "Set up your ConnectApp website",
  "setup.what.portal": "Choose a unique web address where your members can access your church's portal.",
  "setup.why.portal": "Members can use this link to sign in, connect with groups, make donations, and contact your church.",
  "setup.at.portal": "Enter a unique name for your church's web address, then click Save web address.",
  "setup.step.profile": "Your own details",
  "setup.what.profile": "Your record in the church directory: a photo, and a number somebody can reach you on.",
  "setup.why.profile": "Your team is about to meet a directory where you are only a name. Filling yours in is the quickest way to see what you are asking everybody else for.",
  "setup.at.profile": "Press Edit, add a photo and a phone number, and save.",
  "setup.step.teams": "Who serves on the day",
  "setup.what.teams": "Add the teams your church serves in, such as Welcome, Worship and Kids, and the positions on each one.",
  "setup.why.teams": "A team is what a rota is built from. Until one exists there is nobody to schedule, and a volunteer has nothing to accept or decline.",
  "setup.at.teams": "Press Add team, name it the way your church already says it, and list its positions.",
  "setup.step.planTemplate": "Your order of service",
  "setup.what.planTemplate": "A template holding the shape your services usually follow, with each item and how long it runs.",
  "setup.why.planTemplate": "Every service starts from it, so the week's planning becomes editing rather than writing. It also gives your musicians and tech team one order to read from.",
  "setup.at.planTemplate": "Press Add template, then add an item for each part of the service and give it a length.",
  "setup.step.plan": "Plan this week's service",
  "setup.what.plan": "The running order for the service you have coming up, built from your template.",
  "setup.why.plan": "This is the thing your team reads on the day. Doing one now is how you find out whether the template is the right shape before a service day depends on it.",
  "setup.at.plan": "Open the service that says Not planned yet, then start from your template.",
  "setup.step.groupTypes": "The kinds of group you run",
  "setup.what.groupTypes": "The sorts of group your church gathers in: small groups, classes, ministries, whatever you call them.",
  "setup.why.groupTypes": "A group is created as one of these, so until there is at least one kind your church cannot write down a single group.",
  "setup.at.groupTypes": "Press Add group type and name one. You can add the rest as you need them.",
  "setup.step.email": "Send email to your church",
  "setup.what.email": "Connect the account your church sends from, either Resend or your own mail server.",
  "setup.why.email": "Mail from your own account arrives, because it carries your church's name and reputation. The account stays yours, billed to you by your provider.",
  "setup.at.email": "Press Connect and follow it through. We send you a test before anything is written down.",
  "setup.step.giving": "Take a gift online",
  "setup.what.giving": "Connect Stripe, so your congregation can give by card or bank from the portal.",
  "setup.why.giving": "The account is your church's own and the money goes straight into it. Our fee on every gift is zero, and we never hold a penny of it on the way through.",
  "setup.at.giving": "Press Connect via Stripe. It asks for your church's details, which is why the step before this one is worth doing first.",
  "setup.step.funds": "Where gifts go",
  "setup.what.funds": "A fund for each thing your church asks for money towards, beyond the general offering.",
